module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Simplicial.SliceAbelianLowerShriek
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Simplicial.SliceLowerShriekFreeAbelian

/-!
# `j_{p!} j_p^{-1} ℤ_V^♯` in a simplicial degree

Let `(C, J)` be a small site and `K` a simplicial object of `SR(C)`. In simplicial degree `p` the
site `C / K_p` of `CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.situation` carries the topology
`(situation J K).componentTopology p`, which is the componentwise localized topology of the
semi-representable object `K_p` but is *spelled* as the topology generated by the covering
families of the simplicial family of sites. This module reads
`CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable.freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIso` at that spelling, so
that the statement is about the extension by zero
`CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.sliceAbelianLowerShriek` of the simplicial degree.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable.freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIsoOfEq`: the general
  statement at any topology equal to the componentwise localized one.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.sliceFreeYonedaLowerShriekIso`:
  `j_{p!} j_p^{-1} ℤ_V^♯ ≅ ℤ_{h_V × F(K_p)}^♯`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.augmentationComponentFreeYonedaIso`: the same read
  through the total site, `a_! g_{p!} j_p^{-1} ℤ_V^♯ ≅ ℤ_{h_V × F(K_p)}^♯`.

## Implementation notes

The transport is by `subst` on the equality of topologies
`CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.componentTopology_eq`, which is why the general
statement is phrased with the topology as a variable: every typeclass the statement needs is a
`Prop`, so the instances carried along by the substitution and the ones registered at the
componentwise topology are interchangeable.

At the point of application the registered continuity instance is stated for `sliceForget K (op p)`
and the general statement asks for it at `componentOverForget (K.obj (op p))`. The two functors
are definitionally equal — `sliceForget_eq` is `rfl` — but instance search matches on the head
symbol, so the instance is installed by hand.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D87](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D87)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D8B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D8B)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable

attribute [local instance] GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [HasWeakSheafify J (Type u)] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective (Type u)]

/-- **`j_! j^{-1} ℤ_V^♯ = ℤ_{h_V × F(L)}^♯`, at any spelling of the componentwise localized
topology.** This is `freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIso` with the topology on `C / L` taken to
be an arbitrary one equal to `componentwiseTopology J L`, so that it can be read at a site whose
topology is presented differently. -/
def freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIsoOfEq (L : FormalCoproduct.{u} C)
    {T : GrothendieckTopology (ComponentOver L)}
    [(componentOverForget L).IsContinuous T J] (hT : T = componentwiseTopology J L) (V : C) :
    (Functor.sheafPullbackConstruction.sheafPullback (componentOverForget L) AddCommGrpCat.{u}
          T J).obj
        (((componentOverForget L).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u} T J).obj
          (Stacks.Cohomology.CohomologyPresheaf.freeYonedaSheaf J V)) ≅
      (presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        ((yoneda.obj V ⨯ (FormalCoproduct.yoneda (C := C)).obj L) ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free) := by
  subst hT
  exact freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIso J L V

end CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable

namespace CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable

open SemiRepresentable

attribute [local instance] GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  (K : SimplicialObject (FormalCoproduct.{u} C)) [J.toCoverage.HasPullbacks]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective (Type u)]

/-- **`j_{p!} j_p^{-1} ℤ_V^♯ ≅ ℤ_{h_V × F(K_p)}^♯`.** Restricting the free abelian sheaf on a
representable `h_V` to the site `C / K_p` of the simplicial degree `p` and extending it by zero
again gives the free abelian sheaf on the presheaf `h_V × F(K_p)`.

This is Stacks 0D87 part (2) carried across the free abelian sheaf functor
(`CategoryTheory.SemiRepresentable.freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIso`), read at the topology
of the simplicial degree through `componentTopology_eq`. -/
def sliceFreeYonedaLowerShriekIso (p : SimplexCategory) (V : C) :
    (sliceAbelianLowerShriek J K p).obj
        (((sliceForget K (op p)).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u}
          ((situation J K).componentTopology p) J).obj
          (Stacks.Cohomology.CohomologyPresheaf.freeYonedaSheaf J V)) ≅
      (presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        ((yoneda.obj V ⨯ (FormalCoproduct.yoneda (C := C)).obj (K.obj (op p))) ⋙
          AddCommGrpCat.free) :=
  haveI : (componentOverForget (K.obj (op p))).IsContinuous
      ((situation J K).componentTopology p) J := sliceForget_isContinuous J K p
  freeYonedaSheafPushforwardPullbackIsoOfEq J (K.obj (op p)) (componentTopology_eq J K p) V

/-- **`a_! g_{p!} j_p^{-1} ℤ_V^♯ ≅ ℤ_{h_V × F(K_p)}^♯`.** The two isomorphisms combined: the
composite of the component lower shriek `g_{p!}` to the total site with the lower shriek `a_!`
along the augmentation is `j_{p!}` (`componentLowerShriekCompAugmentationAbelianIso`), and
`j_{p!} j_p^{-1} ℤ_V^♯` is the free abelian sheaf on `h_V × F(K_p)`
(`sliceFreeYonedaLowerShriekIso`).

This is the degreewise identification of the terms of the Čech resolution of `a^{-1}ℤ_V^♯` after
applying `a_!`: it exhibits them as the free abelian sheaves on the simplicial object
`K × h_V`. -/
def augmentationComponentFreeYonedaIso (p : SimplexCategory) (V : C) :
    (augmentationAbelianLowerShriek J K).obj
        ((SimplicialSiteSituation.componentLowerShriekAb (situation J K) p).obj
          (((sliceForget K (op p)).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u}
            ((situation J K).componentTopology p) J).obj
            (Stacks.Cohomology.CohomologyPresheaf.freeYonedaSheaf J V))) ≅
      (presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        ((yoneda.obj V ⨯ (FormalCoproduct.yoneda (C := C)).obj (K.obj (op p))) ⋙
          AddCommGrpCat.free) :=
  (componentLowerShriekCompAugmentationAbelianIso J K p).app _ ≪≫
    sliceFreeYonedaLowerShriekIso J K p V

end CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable

end
